# targets/qos.fpr — the QOS backend, as an FP-RISC Struct.
#
# An FP-RISC program that targets QOS (native or portable) instead of
# bare metal or the bytecode VM links against THIS module: one Struct,
# one funnel — every IO obligation goes through Svc.read / Svc.write
# over capability-checked URLs, and the C side underneath it is a HAL
# table (qos/appside/hal.c dispatching qos_hal_t), not an
# implementation the program can reach around.
#
#     QOS = use "../targets/qos".
#     Svc = QOS.Svc.   Caps = QOS.Caps.   IoV constructors likewise.
#
# The Struct itself lives in programs/mods/svc.fpr (content-addressed
# module identity: re-homing the definition would churn every pinned
# hash for zero semantic gain — this file is the profile's named entry
# point, the definition keeps its address).

SVCM = use "../programs/mods/svc".

Svc  = SVCM.Svc.
Caps = SVCM.Caps.
IoV  = SVCM.IoV.
